Revision history for Ham-CW

0.001  2026-10-25
    - Initial release for ITU-R M.1677-1 Morse symbols and operational signals.
    - Control Farnsworth timing and produce timed or sample-based events.
    - Generate tones, PCM WAV audio and standard MIDI files.
    - Use library and command-line interfaces for files, bytes and sample streams.
    - Audio reception is experimental, with multichannel decoding and mark SNR.
    - Include structured errors, diagnostics, POD references and runnable examples.
    - Require Perl 5.20 or later; PDL is an optional numerical backend.
    - Publish complete POD and Markdown docs in a Perl-themed GitHub Pages site.
    - Add isolated peak-RSS benchmarks alongside CPU and wall timings.
    - Keep benchmark fallback reporting valid when optional PDL cannot load.
    - Reduce receiver CPU and memory with complex Goertzel acquisition,
      packed PDL windows, inner products and bounded projection batches.
    - Round event conversions with integer remainders, including exact halves
      and large cumulative boundaries.
    - Let internal reception decoding inherit the configured frame budget.
    - Enforce MIDI byte limits against the complete encoded file size.
    - Add original weekly/manual portability checks for intermediate Perl
      versions, FreeBSD, Solaris and Cygwin, including installed CLI tests.
